---
title: French Press Coffee
image: https://craftcoffeespot.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/French-Press-pour-out-1024x1024.png
time required: 6 minutes
servings: 2
---

Prepare your @coffee{35%g}(coarsely ground). Pour the grounds into your #french press{} and then pour @hot water{525%g}(195°F, approximately obtained by boiling water then letting sit for 30 seconds) over the grounds. Set a timer for ~{4%minutes} from when the water first touches the coffee.

Press the plunger down until the filter is at the top of the water, just enough to keep the grounds submerged. Stir the french press as desired to keep grounds mixing with coffee.

Press the plunger down when your timer goes off and serve immediately.

> The important thing is to preserve a 1g coffee to 15g water ratio.